Keep the score vector the sampling loop already computes, and the AUC
upstream measured over it.

sample() walks 500 diffusion timesteps, computes a per-node score at each one,
measures an AUC against the labels and keeps only np.max over the 500. GraFlag
publishes the scores a method computed rather than recomputing them, so the
vector behind the reported number has to survive the loop -- and so does the
AUC upstream printed for it, which is what `graflag verify` checks the
published scores against.

forward() runs sample() once per trial (20) and prints the mean, std and max
of the per-trial AUCs. Each trial overwrites self.selected_*, so what GraFlag
publishes is the last trial; self.trial_aucs keeps all twenty, so the result
records where that trial sits among them.

Stored on self rather than widened into the return tuple, so the call sites
are untouched.

Nothing about what the method computes changes. The selection rule is still
upstream's -- argmax over the AUCs it printed, measured against the test
labels -- and README.md says plainly what that means for the published number.

